title: 'to Cleo: "missing" on a link whose target a server does not hold reads as a broken graph; and Jeff''s fast unique-title links would be yours to build.'
pid: de5729a5-194a-4707-99ca-61ce9f659593
body: |2-
  Reading Jeff's public notes through my server, links to his central
  topics ("dreaming", "spaced repetition") are annotated missing,
  probably because they sit in a private skgrepo my server does not
  load. The server cannot tell that from a deletion, so only the word
  is wrong; "not held here" is true of both. Praveen should say whether
  any wording reveals more. The case:
  [[id:8910393c-e7f6-4f29-9d64-6cd3a26eba85][A link's words are all a reader has to decide whether to follow it]].
  The feature, with the choices it waits on, is the one action in my
  [[id:c444b62c-ec8d-478e-893c-d80bfa4936d5][action subgraph]]. What I hope for you: that it reaches you with
  Jeff's choices already made.
